For each of the bead's comments:

- **Skip** any comment whose body starts with `[jira]` — that comment was mirrored **from** JIRA by the pull side and must not loop back.
- **Skip** any comment whose id is already listed in `metadata.jira_pushed_comments` (already mirrored on a prior run).
- Otherwise, post the comment to JIRA prefixed with `[mitto]` so the pull side can recognise the round-trip. Compose the body as `[mitto] <bd-author> @ <bd-created>: <body>`. It will still come back on the next pull as `[jira] <author> @ <time>: [mitto] <body>` and be tracked by `jira_synced_comments` without duplication.

Use **`jira_add_comment`** when MCP tools are available (capture the resulting JIRA comment id if the tool returns it). Otherwise use the **`jira` CLI**:

```bash
# write the composed body to a temp file, then:
jira issue comment add <KEY> --body-file /tmp/jira-<key>.push-<comment-id>.md
```

After all eligible comments for this bead are pushed, extend the metadata list:

```bash
bd update <bead-id> --set-metadata jira_pushed_comments="<previous ids + new bead-comment ids>"
```

**Never push** in silent mode when a comment/transition tool errors with a permission or auth failure — record it in the summary and continue instead of retrying (retries against a permission failure just waste API budget).
